{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>That is called the land of Rephaim.</b> I explained above that the intention is ״it shall be called״ and not considered as such in truth, for if you do not say so and it is included among the Rephaim that HaShem gave to Israel, the beraita of the Sifrei is difficult, for they said: ״אֲשֶׁר ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ נוֹתֵן לָךְ״ — this excludes the land across the Jordan that you took on your own, end quote. But is it not included in what HaShem gave? And furthermore, even according to the words of our Rabbis of blessed memory who said in Bereishit Rabbah (ch. 44) that the Rephaim are the Hivites — and we find that Scripture counted them among the seven nations that He gave them when they came up from the land of Egypt, as it is written: ״וָאֹמַר אַעֲלֶה אֶתְכֶם מֵעֳנִי מִצְרַיִם אֶל אֶרֶץ הַכְּנַעֲנִי וְגוֹ׳ וְהַחִוִּי״ (Exodus 3:17) — rather, it is surely so that the land of Og is not reckoned as Rephaim except that they took it on their own." "<b>And if you should say</b>, but do we not find that the Amorite too is mentioned among the seven nations that HaShem said He would give them when they came up from the land of Egypt, and he is Sihon, as it is written (Numbers 21:21): ״מֶלֶךְ הָאֱמֹרִי,״ and it is written (Numbers 21:25): ״וַיֵּשֶׁב יִשְׂרָאֵל בְּעָרֵי הָאֱמֹרִי״ — and our difficulty regarding the words of the Sifrei returns. This is no difficulty, for the cities of the Amorite mentioned regarding Sihon are not what HaShem gave to Abraham, as Scripture explicitly revealed there (Numbers 21:26): ״כִּי חֶשְׁבּוֹן עִיר סִיחוֹן״ and so forth, ״וְהוּא נִלְחַם בְּמֶלֶךְ מוֹאָב הָרִאשׁוֹן וַיִּקַּח אֶת כָּל אַרְצוֹ מִיָּדוֹ״ and so forth — see that the land of Sihon is Moabite, only that Sihon acquired it, and it is called Amorite on account of Sihon, who was king over the Amorites, but it never entered the category of the gift of the seven nations whose time had come." "<b>Further</b>, it appears that whatever is called by the name Rephaim is always included in HaShem's utterance to Abraham: ״וְאֶת הָרְפָאִים״ (Genesis 15:20), and the land of Sihon and Og is included in what HaShem gave, for Scripture called it the land of the Amorite, and the land of Og too — Scripture called it Rephaim, who are the Hivites. And the meaning of the beraita of the Sifrei, which said that the exclusion of the land across the Jordan (referring to Deuteronomy 7:13) concerns the settling of the land, is that although HaShem gave seven nations to Abraham, not all lands are equal in this matter of being fit for dwelling. And this is like the matter of the holiness of the land itself, for we find ten degrees of holiness in the land itself in its various places (Kelim 1:6), and the land of Sihon and Og would be a lower degree. And although HaShem gave it to Abraham, it would be as spoil along with it, and the substance of the land would be like the rest of the spoil or for desolation, but not for dwelling." "<b>And this</b> is what they said in the Sifrei: ״לָתֶת לָנוּ״ — this excludes the land across the Jordan. There Scripture was precise to say: ״בָּאתִי אֶל הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּע ה׳ לָתֶת לָנוּ״ (Deuteronomy 6:23) — meaning, the land that HaShem swore He would give us for our dwelling, excluding the other lands which, though He gave them to us, He did not give the land for dwelling because it is not fit for holiness. And you will find that He also gave Ammon and Moab and Edom, who are the Kenite and the Kenizzite and the Kadmonite, and it is written (Jeremiah 49:17): ״וְהָיְתָה אֱדוֹם לְשַׁמָּה,״ and similarly the land of Sihon and Og was fit to be. But the land of Israel is what HaShem swore to give to Israel to dwell there. And keep for yourself this principle too: that even though HaShem did not give the land for dwelling in it, and even though He did not give it along with the rest to Abraham and the majority of Israel conquered it — one must treat it with the law of holiness because it was conquered before HaShem."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:51.592120076Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}